Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Diachronic Word Embeddings", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"733b1376-82b8-4563-9202-4ec561467b33"],

Cell["\<\
200 Years of Semantic Drift, Traced Through a Word-Embedding Space\
\>", "Subtitle",ExpressionUUID->"420bb7ab-ae78-49e0-bf5f-17eb82de0bc1"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Setup", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"7d507359-e974-4d50-8d94-c2bec39e560d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "All of this notebook's code lives in the package ",
 StyleBox["wolfram/DiachronicEmbeddings.wl",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ". Evaluate the cell below first; it ",
 "loads the package, which in turn reads the small committed data products in \
",
 StyleBox["data/",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " (the 1.6 GB raw HistWords embeddings are not needed). Every figure ",
 "and table further down is then produced by a single call to a package \
function."
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{50, 50}, {6, 
  6}},ExpressionUUID->"6bde4f6f-8691-4e6d-a278-7b85528ccff1"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Get", "[", 
  RowBox[{"FileNameJoin", "[", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"If", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"$Notebooks", "&&", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Quiet", "[", 
          RowBox[{"NotebookDirectory", "[", "]"}], "]"}], "=!=", 
         "$Failed"}]}], ",", 
       RowBox[{"ParentDirectory", "[", 
        RowBox[{"NotebookDirectory", "[", "]"}], "]"}], 
       ",", "\"\</Users/user/GitHub/DiachronicWordEmbeddings\>\""}], "]"}], 
     ",", "\"\<wolfram\>\"", ",", "\"\<DiachronicEmbeddings.wl\>\""}], "}"}], 
   "]"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellMargins->{{50, 30}, {8, 8}},
 FontSize->12,
 CellLabel->" In[1]:=",ExpressionUUID->"85355cc0-ccf7-4d30-b010-f8dbdc192043"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"deHero", "[", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellMargins->{{50, 30}, {8, 8}},
 FontSize->12,
 CellLabel->" In[2]:=",ExpressionUUID->"104834b6-7563-4162-b53e-953fcfeecd03"],

Cell[OutputFormData["\<\
Labeled[-Graphics-   -Graphics-   -Graphics-, 1800s -Graphics- 1990s, Bottom]

        -Graphics-   -Graphics-   -Graphics-\
\>"], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.989148235572974*^9},
 CellLabel->" Out[2]=",ExpressionUUID->"e36f893a-8d0c-43a0-adca-f23a8d7c2874"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Figure. ",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 "Six words, two centuries. Each panel projects one word's per-decade ",
 "vector \[Dash] blue in the 1800s, red in the 1990s \[Dash] into a 2-D map \
of its own ",
 "changing neighbourhood. \[Section]5 lets you explore any of the fourteen \
words ",
 "interactively."
}], "Caption",
 CellMargins->{{55, 55}, {2, 
  16}},ExpressionUUID->"0941788c-59a0-4f91-9a0f-a9d12a6e9a45"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Word meanings move. ",
 StyleBox["Gay",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " once meant carefree; ",
 StyleBox["broadcast",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " meant to scatter seed by hand; a ",
 StyleBox["computer",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " was a person who did ",
 "arithmetic. This notebook makes that motion visible and measurable. Using \
the ",
 StyleBox["HistWords",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " embeddings (word2vec / SGNS trained on the Google N-grams ",
 "English corpus, one model per decade from the 1800s to the 1990s), we bring \
two ",
 "centuries of independently-trained vector spaces into a single comparable \
frame ",
 "with ",
 StyleBox["orthogonal Procrustes alignment",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 ", then trace individual words ",
 "as ",
 StyleBox["trajectories",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " through a 2-D projection of that shared space."
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{60, 60}, {8, 10}},
 FontSize->14,
 Background->RGBColor[
  0.96, 0.97, 1.],ExpressionUUID->"79ab17a4-1324-4baf-ab3a-a88bfd16176c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The drifting paths are the heart of the post (and \[Section]5 turns ",
 "them into an interactive explorer). We then test, on the same aligned \
embeddings, the ",
 "two ",
 StyleBox["statistical laws of semantic change",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " of Hamilton, Leskovec & Jurafsky ",
 "(2016): the law of conformity (frequent words drift more slowly) replicates \
cleanly, ",
 "while the law of innovation (polysemous words drift faster) turns out to be \
a frequency ",
 "confound in this corpus \[Dash] a useful reminder to control before \
concluding. ",
 "Everything is computed in the Wolfram Language; the code and data are in \
the companion ",
 "repository."
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{60, 60}, {8, 10}},
 FontSize->14,
 Background->RGBColor[
  0.96, 0.97, 1.],ExpressionUUID->"86971816-efd8-4ae0-a31e-f35274a464a9"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["1. The idea: words as moving points", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"845690a2-070c-4046-84a7-de132b78f3cc"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A ",
 StyleBox["word embedding",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " places every word at a point in a ",
 "high-dimensional space so that words appearing in similar contexts land \
close ",
 "together. Cosine similarity between two vectors then behaves like a \
similarity of ",
 "meaning: in a modern embedding, ",
 StyleBox["king",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " sits near ",
 StyleBox["queen",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["throne",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 ", far from ",
 StyleBox["pizza",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{50, 50}, {6, 
  6}},ExpressionUUID->"4bbb8add-8abb-4eb3-93dc-e88200f5aeef"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Now train one embedding on text from the 1850s and another on text from ",
 "the 1990s. A word whose meaning has changed will sit in a different \
neighbourhood ",
 "on the two maps. ",
 StyleBox["Gay",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " keeps company with ",
 StyleBox["cheerful, merry, lively",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " in the 1850s and with ",
 StyleBox["homosexual, lesbian, bisexual",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " in the 1990s. If we can line the two maps up, that change becomes a \
displacement we ",
 "can draw \[Dash] and across twenty decades, a path."
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{50, 50}, {6, 
  6}},ExpressionUUID->"bd9974d2-a470-4f2a-8cc8-e9b860829d57"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Takeaway.  ",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 "Meaning change shows up as a word ",
 StyleBox["moving",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " relative to the rest of the vocabulary. The whole project is about \
measuring and ",
 "drawing that motion honestly."
}], "Text",
 CellFrame->{{3, 0}, {0, 0}},
 CellMargins->{{60, 60}, {8, 12}},
 CellFrameColor->RGBColor[0.35, 0.6, 0.4],
 FontSize->12,
 Background->RGBColor[
  0.93, 0.97, 0.93],ExpressionUUID->"454bea17-f47c-4399-b4e5-926ecb7a870b"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["2. The data: HistWords decade embeddings", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"d36a3d96-ab06-4b36-8f11-ea2b1895dd41"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "We use the ",
 StyleBox["HistWords",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " embeddings of Hamilton et al.: ",
 "300-dimensional skip-gram-with-negative-sampling (SGNS) vectors, trained \
separately ",
 "for each decade on the Google N-grams ",
 StyleBox["eng-all",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " corpus, from the 1800s ",
 "through the 1990s \[Dash] twenty decade-models, each with a 100,000-word \
vocabulary. ",
 "The vectors are L2-normalized; a word absent from a decade is stored as a \
zero vector ",
 "and skipped. The raw download is ~1.6 GB and is not committed; a thin \
Python shim ",
 "converts the NumPy/pickle files to plain float32 binaries, and everything \
downstream ",
 "is Wolfram Language."
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{50, 50}, {6, 
  6}},ExpressionUUID->"ad8c8275-883c-4646-8d21-4822bdefd5ee"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Coverage varies by word. Of the fourteen we track, ",
 StyleBox["gay",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["awful",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["literally",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["nice",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["mouse",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["web",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " appear in all twenty decades; ",
 StyleBox["queer",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " from the 1830s, ",
 StyleBox["broadcast",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " from the 1850s, and ",
 StyleBox["computer",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " at 1900 (the human-\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]computer\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] \
sense) ",
 "then continuously from the 1940s (the machine). Gaps are drawn as dashed \
segments. ",
 "The full word list is ",
 StyleBox["deWords[]",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{50, 50}, {6, 
  6}},ExpressionUUID->"8b354501-ccbc-40bc-b0bd-5df082cc0dda"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["3. Why the decades must be aligned", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"c9bcf0d8-6814-4f30-af2e-20566b986868"],

Cell["\<\
Each decade's embedding is trained independently, so its coordinate axes are \
arbitrary: two decade-maps can be rotated and reflected relative to one \
another even when they agree perfectly about which words are near which. (A \
skip-gram objective is invariant under any orthogonal transformation of the \
space, so nothing pins down a shared orientation.) Before a word can be \
tracked through time, the decades must be rotated into a common frame.\
\>", "Text",
 CellMargins->{{50, 50}, {6, 
  6}},ExpressionUUID->"7678cf58-bbb2-419f-98c7-b90a8a52353a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "We use ",
 StyleBox["orthogonal Procrustes alignment",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 ". Let ",
 StyleBox["A",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " hold the vectors of the 5,000 highest-frequency words present in every \
decade, for ",
 "one decade, and ",
 StyleBox["B",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " the same words in the 1990s reference. We seek the ",
 "orthogonal ",
 StyleBox["R",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " minimising"
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{50, 50}, {6, 
  6}},ExpressionUUID->"33d1f3f3-237a-4160-a540-da9b4adb583c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   UnderscriptBox["argmin", 
    StyleBox["R",
     FontSlant->Italic]], " ", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
    "\[LeftDoubleBracketingBar]", "A", " ", "R", " ", "-", " ", "B", 
     "\[RightDoubleBracketingBar]"}], "2"], " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"subject", "\[ThinSpace]", "to"}], " ", 
    SuperscriptBox["R", "T"], "R", "=", "I"}]}], 
  TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellMargins->{{80, 50}, {8, 
  8}},ExpressionUUID->"7b202f0e-547d-4f01-bf97-70279be8a553"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This has a closed form from a singular value decomposition: if ",
 StyleBox["U S V",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 "\[Transpose] = ",
 StyleBox["A",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 "\[Transpose]",
 StyleBox["B",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 ", then ",
 StyleBox["R",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " = ",
 StyleBox["U V",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 "\[Transpose]",
 ". Because ",
 StyleBox["R",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " is orthogonal it preserves every length and angle ",
 StyleBox["within",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " a decade \[Dash] it only reorients the space \[Dash] so each decade's \
nearest ",
 "neighbours are exactly as trained, while becoming comparable ",
 StyleBox["across",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " decades. (Nearest-neighbour queries in \[Section]6 are therefore run in \
each ",
 "decade's own native space; alignment is needed only to compare frames.)"
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{50, 50}, {6, 
  6}},ExpressionUUID->"81aaa4d7-8c77-425c-b260-13310e933858"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"deAlignmentPlot", "[", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellMargins->{{50, 30}, {8, 8}},
 FontSize->12,
 CellLabel->" In[3]:=",ExpressionUUID->"b953d7d6-5515-4b3f-8e7e-6ec4ee7dd76a"],

Cell[OutputFormData["\<\
                                                             7
Legended[-Graphics-, Placed[LineLegend[{Directive[PointSize[---], 
                                                            360
 
>       AbsoluteThickness[2], RGBColor[0.13, 0.34, 0.68], Thickness[0.006]], 
 
                            7
>      Directive[PointSize[---], AbsoluteThickness[2], 
                           360
 
>       RGBColor[0.85, 0.16, 0.11], Thickness[0.006]]}, 
 
>     {raw (independently trained), after Procrustes alignment}, 
 
>     LegendMarkers -> {{-Graphics-, Offset[8]}, {-Graphics-, Offset[8]}}, 
 
>     Joined -> {True, True}, LabelStyle -> {}, LegendLayout -> Column], 
 
>    {0.32, 0.82}, Identity]]\
\>"], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.9891482358554783`*^9},
 CellLabel->" Out[3]=",ExpressionUUID->"d9ccfb58-9323-4a7f-a7a4-82f94ce5a783"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Figure. ",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 "Mean cosine of the 5,000 shared anchor words to their 1990s vectors, ",
 "before (blue) and after (red) Procrustes alignment. Alignment lifts the \
curve at ",
 "every decade; both necessarily reach 1.0 at the 1990s reference."
}], "Caption",
 CellMargins->{{55, 55}, {2, 
  16}},ExpressionUUID->"b54af557-6f5a-478e-9da4-68be7a0bff3a"],

Cell["\<\
How far from comparable are the raw spaces? The rotation that best aligns the \
1800s onto the 1990s is large: \[LeftDoubleBracketingBar]R \[Minus] I\
\[RightDoubleBracketingBar] = 21.20. For calibration, two unrelated 300-D \
spaces are related by a random rotation with \[LeftDoubleBracketingBar]R \
\[Minus] I\[RightDoubleBracketingBar] \[TildeTilde] 24.50, identical spaces \
give 0, and a perfect mirror-flip gives the maximum 34.60. So the 1800s axes \
begin almost as unrelated to the 1990s as random \[Dash] alignment is \
essential, not cosmetic \[Dash] and the required rotation then shrinks \
smoothly toward the present.\
\>", "Text",
 CellMargins->{{50, 50}, {6, 
  6}},ExpressionUUID->"b48e497e-fb87-4b52-8244-1a99a16dc850"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Aligning lifts the mean anchor-word cosine to the 1990s at every decade ",
 "(1800s: ",
 "0.42",
 " \[Rule] ",
 "0.57",
 "; 1900s: ",
 "0.50",
 " \[Rule] ",
 "0.65",
 "). That the raw (blue) curve already rises, rather than sitting near zero, \
is itself ",
 "informative: HistWords initialises each decade's training from the previous \
one, so ",
 "adjacent decades inherit a partial common orientation \[Dash] but that \
shared frame ",
 "erodes over a century, which is exactly why distant decades must be \
re-aligned. The ",
 "numbers above come from ",
 StyleBox["deAlignmentFacts[]",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{50, 50}, {6, 
  6}},ExpressionUUID->"1c46ad6f-e073-429f-b07d-373c99a9dd24"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Takeaway.  ",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 "Independently trained spaces are not comparable as shipped. One ",
 "orthogonal rotation per decade, fitted on stable high-frequency words, \
makes them ",
 "comparable while leaving each decade's internal geometry untouched."
}], "Text",
 CellFrame->{{3, 0}, {0, 0}},
 CellMargins->{{60, 60}, {8, 12}},
 CellFrameColor->RGBColor[0.35, 0.6, 0.4],
 FontSize->12,
 Background->RGBColor[
  0.93, 0.97, 0.93],ExpressionUUID->"1db301a2-1e5f-4ea1-9e85-b044f545cdfc"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["4. How to read a trajectory", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"314217b9-3e41-4699-9b9b-0ac5c4717858"],

Cell["\<\
For one word we collect its aligned vector in every decade it occurs, gather \
the nearest neighbours that anchor each era of its meaning, and project that \
whole local neighbourhood to two dimensions with PCA. The word's path then \
threads between an early-meaning cluster and a late-meaning cluster; colour \
runs from blue (1800s) to red (1990s). One call draws any word:\
\>", "Text",
 CellMargins->{{50, 50}, {6, 
  6}},ExpressionUUID->"8ddc95cb-51c2-4344-b229-7076ffd4cda5"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"deTrajectoryPlot", "[", "\"\<gay\>\"", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellMargins->{{50, 30}, {8, 8}},
 FontSize->12,
 CellLabel->" In[4]:=",ExpressionUUID->"6b7749c2-6140-48f6-bd24-9af7f2feca69"],

Cell[OutputFormData["\<\
-Graphics-\
\>"], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.989148235861082*^9},
 CellLabel->" Out[4]=",ExpressionUUID->"47e19622-6b17-40a6-92ea-61cd233bf265"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Figure. ",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 StyleBox["gay",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 ": the path lingers among ",
 StyleBox["merry, cheerful, joyous, lively, gaiety",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " through the blue and purple decades, ",
 "then swings sharply red-ward to ",
 StyleBox["homosexual, lesbian, gays, bisexual",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " by the 1990s \[Dash] a two-century meaning change rendered as a single \
sweep."
}], "Caption",
 CellMargins->{{55, 55}, {2, 
  16}},ExpressionUUID->"43fc7994-cba4-4f32-84be-fbd1f624f1fb"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["What the projection does and does not say.",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " The 2-D layout is a ",
 StyleBox["per-word",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " PCA of that word's own cloud, chosen to spread its motion across ",
 "the page; absolute positions and the axes themselves carry no global \
meaning, and 2-D ",
 "distances are an approximation of the true 300-D ones. The trustworthy \
signal is ",
 StyleBox["which neighbours sit at each end",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " of the path and ",
 StyleBox["how far the word travels between them",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " \[Dash] both of which come straight ",
 "from the high-dimensional cosine geometry, not the projection."
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{50, 50}, {6, 
  6}},ExpressionUUID->"4246dae5-bbba-445d-b1a5-ef1bfc776a83"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Takeaway.  ",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 "Read a trajectory by its ",
 StyleBox["endpoints and their neighbours",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 ", not by the exact shape of the curve. The neighbours are the evidence; the \
curve is ",
 "just their geometry."
}], "Text",
 CellFrame->{{3, 0}, {0, 0}},
 CellMargins->{{60, 60}, {8, 12}},
 CellFrameColor->RGBColor[0.35, 0.6, 0.4],
 FontSize->12,
 Background->RGBColor[
  0.93, 0.97, 0.93],ExpressionUUID->"9ad38d22-fb40-4def-b22c-b8a6cfd3d9ae"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["5. Explore all fourteen words", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"9319baa3-794d-476f-bfb6-e060923ea589"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Rather than print fourteen separate plots, the same construction is wired \
",
 "into one interactive ",
 StyleBox["Manipulate",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ". Pick a word, scrub the time slider to ",
 "reveal the path decade by decade, and toggle the neighbour labels. (In the \
live ",
 "notebook this is fully interactive; the static view shows ",
 StyleBox["gay",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " with its full path.)"
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{50, 50}, {6, 
  6}},ExpressionUUID->"0e8b8e35-d19d-4ac2-a14e-8b209b871aa4"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"deExplorer", "[", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellMargins->{{50, 30}, {8, 8}},
 FontSize->12,
 CellLabel->" In[5]:=",ExpressionUUID->"34335b1e-2c78-4c47-abbe-42e7d2aa4d95"],

Cell[OutputFormData["\<\
Manipulate[deTrajectoryPlot[DiachronicEmbeddings`Private`word, 
 
>    DiachronicEmbeddings`Private`yearMax, 
 
>    DiachronicEmbeddings`Private`neighbourLabels], 
 
>   {{DiachronicEmbeddings`Private`word, gay, word}, 
 
>    {gay, broadcast, computer, awful, queer, literally, terrific, guy, 
 
>     media, fun, cell, nice, mouse, web}}, 
 
>   {{DiachronicEmbeddings`Private`yearMax, 1990, reveal decades up to}, 
 
>    1800, 1990, 10, Appearance -> Labeled}, 
 
>   {{DiachronicEmbeddings`Private`neighbourLabels, True, neighbour labels}, 
 
>    {True, False}}, ControlPlacement -> Top, SaveDefinitions -> True]\
\>"], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.989148235864386*^9},
 CellLabel->" Out[5]=",ExpressionUUID->"492d08f0-7315-465c-8528-9a347f7946ad"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A few worth visiting: ",
 StyleBox["broadcast",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " (agricultural ",
 StyleBox["sow / seed / scatter",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " \[Rule] ",
 StyleBox["radio / television / bbc",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 "); ",
 StyleBox["computer",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " (a V from human surnames through ",
 StyleBox["electronic / circuits",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " to ",
 StyleBox["software / internet",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 "); ",
 StyleBox["mouse",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " (keeps ",
 StyleBox["rat / cat",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " but grows a second ",
 StyleBox["cursor / click / keyboard",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " cluster); ",
 StyleBox["web",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " (spider \[Rule] ",
 StyleBox["www / browser / server",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 "); ",
 StyleBox["terrific",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["awful",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " (the two halves of a terror-to-praise swap); and ",
 StyleBox["guy",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " (the Guy Fawkes effigy \[Rule] ",
 StyleBox["fellow / chap / dude",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 ")."
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{50, 50}, {6, 
  6}},ExpressionUUID->"0c3052e7-5440-43a3-9cb6-4686dd712ab1"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["6. Nearest-neighbour drift tables", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"ce37e0a1-61a4-40e7-95a7-716729b0ae89"],

Cell["\<\
The trajectories are the geometry of a simpler fact: the list of a word's \
nearest neighbours turns over from decade to decade. Neighbours are computed \
by cosine similarity in each decade's own native space. Sampled every fifty \
years:\
\>", "Text",
 CellMargins->{{50, 50}, {6, 
  6}},ExpressionUUID->"73b250cb-b032-4076-819a-14be48f1eafc"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"deNeighborTable", "[", 
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<gay\>\"", ",", "\"\<broadcast\>\"", ",", "\"\<awful\>\"", 
    ",", "\"\<computer\>\"", ",", "\"\<guy\>\"", ",", "\"\<terrific\>\"", 
    ",", "\"\<media\>\"", ",", "\"\<queer\>\""}], "}"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellMargins->{{50, 30}, {8, 8}},
 FontSize->12,
 CellLabel->" In[6]:=",ExpressionUUID->"731ed675-532d-43e1-b2eb-e6d007d78adf"],

